 \reply
-We have added SQLRight as a baseline in RQ2. \TODO{supported target DBMSs, adaptation, campaign setting, and results of SQLRight}
+We have added SQLRight as a baseline in RQ2. Since SQLRight officially supports only SQLite, PostgreSQL, and MySQL, we have adapted it to the four target DBMSs while keeping its AFL-based queue scheduling, AST-based mutator, and oracle framework, and we have included the adaptation code in our artifact. The results can be found in \metareviewref{3}.
+
 
 We have also extended the related work in Section~VI with SQLRight, sqllogictest, and seed-selection techniques. SQLRight performs coverage-guided DBMS fuzzing for logic bugs, whereas \tool{} constructs initial seeds for DBMS fuzzers. sqllogictest validates query results across database engines with a shared test format, whereas \tool{} transfers test cases into seeds for coverage-guided fuzzing. Seed-selection and scheduling techniques, such as corpus minimization and power schedules (e.g., AFLFast), choose or prioritize seeds within an existing corpus, whereas \tool{} constructs the initial corpus for target DBMSs that lack one; the two directions are therefore orthogonal and can be combined.
 
-The updated Table~III and Table~IV with the SQLRight and SmartFuzz columns are shown in \metareviewref{3}.
 
